# The phone's environment. Copy to `apps/mobile/.env` and fill in what you need.
#
# Everything here is `EXPO_PUBLIC_`, which means two things worth knowing before
# you put anything in this file:
#
#   1. It is **baked into the bundle at build time** by the Metro transform, not
#      read at runtime. Changing a value needs `expo start --clear` locally and a
#      fresh build for a release — an edit alone changes nothing, and the app
#      goes on running with whatever it was compiled with.
#   2. It is **public**. Anyone with the app can read these. Nothing that grants
#      anything belongs here; those live on the API. See the repo-root
#      `.env.example`.

# Where the API is. Only development needs this: a release build points at
# api.daysofar.com, and a phone is not the machine running your server, so
# `localhost` resolves to the phone itself and every request fails looking like
# the server is down. With this unset in development the app guesses the Expo
# packager's own host, which is by definition the machine you ran `expo start`
# on — usually right, and this is the override for when it is not.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:4000

# --- Billing ---
# RevenueCat's *public SDK key*, one per platform, from Project settings → Apps
# → (your app) in their dashboard. Public by design: it identifies the app and
# grants nothing on its own, which is what makes `EXPO_PUBLIC_` right for it
# rather than a leak. The webhook secret, which does grant something, lives only
# on the API.
#
# Take the key from the app entry matching the platform — an iOS key starts
# `appl_` and an Android one `goog_`. Crossing them over does not fail loudly:
# the SDK configures, `getOfferings()` comes back empty, and the paywall reports
# that the store has nothing on sale.
#
# With both unset the app is fully usable and the paywall says it cannot reach a
# store. That is the ordinary state of a simulator and of any build pointed at a
# local API, not a misconfiguration.
#
# Note that purchases do not work in Expo Go at all — the SDK falls back to
# "Browser Mode" and logs so. Testing a real checkout needs a development build.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_
